o-chinese-border-city-via-newly-opened-bridge/a-79748580?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korean leader Kim Jong Un travelled to China’s border city of Dandong via a newly opened bridge linking the two countries, where he met a senior Chinese official.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why Russia's arrest of Japanese journalist is the latest sign of deteriorating ties between the countries.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11c6ec277e6244942a819695ece1f5f33e32e34bcea49b15d1d177397a1773d3</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T05:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-russia-s-arrest-of-japanese-journalist-is-the-latest-sign-of-deteriorating-ties-between-the-coun/a-79742995--e6439f04b25d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-russia-s-arrest-of-japanese-journalist-is-the-latest-sign-of-deteriorating-ties-between-the-countries/a-79742995?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Japan is demanding access to a journalist who was arrested by Russian security services. The Kremlin claims that Japan is using journalists as spies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Taiwan: Typhoon Champi leaves 1 dead, over 500 injured</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:280ee26fcfd56cc092fb3d8a14c54945e9568eee4ef2d0d586cb307ea901755f</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T05:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/taiwan-typhoon-champi-leaves-1-dead-over-500-injured/a-79748221--2c62bf3b9cf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/taiwan-typhoon-champi-leaves-1-dead-over-500-injured/a-79748221?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After killing one person and causing major disruptions in Taiwan, Typhoon Champi is now headed towards China.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Afghan women could lose one of their last paths to a higher education</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23ee61298fce44bf939a45f5368b7bf18f9730f4f5cf36df5a98d6aef572e826</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghan-women-could-lose-one-of-their-last-paths-to-a-higher-education/a-79745173--2a76364e2679.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghan-women-could-lose-one-of-their-last-paths-to-a-higher-education/a-79745173?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has defunded one of the last universities giving Afghan women the chance to receive an education after the Taliban takeover in 2021. DW spoke with a student who says she's lost hope of ever earning a degree.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sri Lanka: Death of iconic elephant raises habitat concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afddc25fd313efa59c8a922cf1f11d68b5a104a20dbda788153949fbdcba3259</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-death-of-iconic-elephant-raises-habitat-concerns/a-79735669--6048c81cd2f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-death-of-iconic-elephant-raises-habitat-concerns/a-79735669?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of what was thought to be Sri Lanka’s largest elephant has drawn attention to human-elephant conflict in rural communities. The island country sees a high number of deadly encounters.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb241807f107024ba74b3825f2aa8948b0e8328bc317d645f513c3383d45ef0b</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877--83771c04f78a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the women powering India's youth-led 'Cockroach' protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6a9c40dd754703cd229bef7547028e2825ba7893d4758eaa415a4ea4bd45cd7</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824--e78a361757e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing online harassment and police detentions, women are taking to the streets of Indian cities in large numbers for the youth-led "Cockroach" protests. Amid a large-scale crackdown, they refuse to be seen as victims.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Brutal, revolutionary empire builder: Genghis Khan's legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60a6a61174d241e9be2370cee6bcba64de1ea54653965ea96e3c4c51802b9b54</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T08:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112--675146225486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin is host to a major exhibition on the founder of the Mongol Empire and his successors. Here's how Genghis Khan disrupted the course of history.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar refugees find hope in Thailand's work program</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f5fd316c9435e792a015903c08688e39ead8b329e23ca575e4ef277dcc70625</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921--572ae4634b5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A year ago, Thailand granted long-staying refugees from Myanmar the right to work legally. Refugees and rights groups welcome the move but say the program's first year has exposed significant shortcomings.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
